BUGS 9-12 (all Low) — remaining unpinned / stale self-descriptions after the cycle-3 ruling.
Grouped: each is a one-line strike or a one-line correction. None is a false green.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BUG 9 — "the tally is printed on EVERY path that reaches a verdict" has a SECOND,
        undocumented exception at exit 4.

  base-descent-check.sh L116-119:
    #   Every invariant is printed, and the `-- result:` tally line with it, on every
    #   path that reaches a verdict — including exit 1 and exit 4 [C22]. A usage error
    #   (exit 2) is the documented exception: it exits before any operand is resolved,
    #   so there is nothing to tally.

  L334 exits 4 — a documented VERDICT code — printing no invariants and no tally:
    command -v git >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "... git not found — NOTHING WAS ASSERTED
      (this is not a pass)" >&2; exit 4; }

  $ env PATH=/nonexistent-dir /bin/bash base-descent-check.sh --key FOO --runs-dir /tmp
  base-descent-check: git not found — NOTHING WAS ASSERTED (this is not a pass)
  exit=4      has '-- result:'?  NO

  C22 pins the claim only for the two paths it exercises (exit 1 via C2's fixture, exit 4
  via C4's), so the pin is NARROWER than the sentence — the cycle-1/cycle-2 pattern exactly.
  Practically unreachable (no git = the script can do nothing) and it is not a green.
  FIX: name the git-absent path as a second exception, or say "every path that resolves an
  operand".

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BUG 10 — the deleted corpus statistic "516 of 898" survives in the change-set's OTHER
         artifacts, and is now wrong.

  $ grep -c '516 of 898' tasks/recovery/NEARS-1806-wiring.diff
  3            (diff line 75 prose, line 214 = the [6] prose it installs,
                line 236 = workflow.json R8; line 223's [9b] prose carries "516 run files")
  docs/solutions/NEARS-1806-base-descent-guard.md:46  "516 of 898 run files record `base`
                as a branch NAME"

  Re-measured with the guard header's own census method, 2026-08-11, tasks/runs/*.json:
    905 files, 899 parseable — base=SHA 333 · base=BRANCH NAME 517 · base absent 49.
    => the live figure is 517 of 899, not 516 of 898.

  The guard itself handles this correctly (the number was pulled from runtime output and
  the surviving census is dated + carries its reproduction command). The wiring diff does
  not — and it is the artifact that BECOMES normative workflow prose when applied, in three
  places. Applying it installs a stale statistic as a live fact in [6], [9b] and R8.
  FIX: date the number in the diff and the doc, or replace it with "the majority of run
  files" + the reproduction command, as the guard header already does.

