BUG 12 — surviving RUNTIME-OUTPUT coverage claims with zero pins (the ruling's letter).

  a) "$n_unresolvable SHA(s) did not resolve ... The stale count is therefore a FLOOR,
      not a total."                       (L608-610)
     $ grep -c 'FLOOR, not a total' base-descent-check.test.sh  ->  0
     TRUE, but nothing reddens if it stops being true. It is a statement about what this
     run proved — precisely the sentence class the ruling covers.

  b) "DEGRADED: run file <state> ... zero keys could be read."   (L602-604)
     $ grep -c 'DEGRADED: run file' base-descent-check.test.sh  ->  0
     Reached by C7's fixture (absent run file) but never asserted.

  c) The phase matrix row "[7] [8]  I-1 required · I-2 required · I-3 n/a" (L265) carries
     no pin. ([6] -> C20, [9b] -> C1, and "I-3 n/a at 7" is incidentally pinned by C13
     since a 9b-scoped I-3 would make C13 exit 4 instead of 0. "I-2 required at [7]/[8]"
     and all of [8] are unexercised.)

  d) "Each ADJACENT pair in that chain is pinned" for `2 > 1 > 4 > 3 > 5 > 0` (L112-114)
     enumerates FOUR pairs; the chain has FIVE. The fifth (5 > 0) IS pinned — C3 exits 5
     on a fixture that would otherwise be 0 — but it is not cited, so the enumeration
     under-reports its own coverage. Cosmetic; the claim itself holds.

  FIX: pin (a) and (b) with one assert_contains each, add a phase-7/8 case for (c), cite
  C3 for (d) — or delete the sentences, per the ruling.
